{
	title: 'Notice text from the model: a <summary> ends a final answer',
	spec: "SYSTEM.md asks the model to end a final answer with <summary>…</summary>: one line under 80 characters saying what happened. common/summary.ts extracts it and hides it: both clients draw a text block without its summary tags, and while the answer streams they also hide an unclosed tag and a trailing prefix of '<summary>', so no part of the tag ever flashes. A notice (task qm) shows the summary instead of the reply's last line (no tag: the last line of the text without tags), and a push for a completed turn reads 'done: <summary>'. A tag, not a tool: a tool call at the end of a turn would cost another request.",
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['qm']
}
